   |                                                                       |
   |                                                    O V E R - V I E W  |
   l_ __ __________________________________________________________________j

   Say  you  are  a  THrobbing-Grissle  WHQ.    All  THG  releases are to be
   free-downloads  on  your board, but it gets a bit tedious having to use a
   FreeDL-maker  utility  every  time one gets uploaded.  (THG is a prolific
   group, you see.)  You then decide to use noC-AutoFree and configure it to
   watch for uploads with the prefix 'THG-' and automatically make them free
   to download.  Life is then MUCH more enjoyable at the THG WHQ.

    _ __ __________________________________________________________________
                                                                           |
                                                  I N S T A L L A T I O N  ¦
            _ __ __________________________________________________________j

   To  install  noC-AutoFree, first copy the main program, "AutoFree" to your
   "C:"  directory.  You must have the ReqTools library installed in 'LIBS:'.
   Next  you  must  create  a  configuration  file,  "S:AutoFree.config".   A
   template  has  been  included in the package.  AutoFree can be run up to 9
   times, with separate configurations.  The '.x' after each config parameter
   should  be  replaced  with  the  configuration  number  you  are defining.
   Following are the options you may set:

   CONFPATH.x:
   Use this to set the path of the conference you want AutoFree to be active
   in.       This    parameter    is    REQUIRED    to    be set.  (Example:
   'CONFPATH.1=BBS:elite/')

   FILEPREFIX.x:
   Files  uploaded  with the filename-prefix defined here will automatically
   become  free downloads.  This parameter is REQUIRED to be set.  (Example:
   'FILEPREFIX.1=THG-'  ...   meaning if a file 'THG-FOO.lha' is uploaded it
   will become free, while 'THGENER.lha' will not.)

   FREEDLTEXT.x:
   You  may  set the text appended to file descriptions of files meeting the
   above  FILEPREFIX.    This will automatically be indented 35 characters.
   ANSI  codes  may  be  used.  This is not a required parameter.  (Example:
   'FREEDLTEXT.1=>>> FrEe DoWnLoAd!!!')

   UPLOADPATH.x:
   If  the conference's upload path is not simply CONFNAME + 'upload/', you
   must define the path here. (Example: 'UPLOADPATH.1=UL:')

    _ __ __________________________________________________________________
                                                                           |
                                                                U S A G E  |
            _ __ __________________________________________________________j


   It  is suggested that you run AutoFree from your startup-sequence so that
   it  will  be  in  memory  after a reboot.  Following are some examples of
   usage.

             'AUTOFREE 2'   - Run autofree with configuration #2.
             'AUTOFREE 2 K' - Terminate autofree config'ed #2.

   If  you  have  several conferences you want this utility to be active in,
   simply  run  AutoFree  as  many times  as  needed with different configs.
   AutoFree  installs  itself  in the background as a ready-waiting process,
   (IE  no  CPU time is used until it actually does some work), and detaches
   itself from the CLI process.

   AutoFree  is  NOT  a  door.   It is a resident task, (or tasks if you use
   multiple  configs),  which  watches   for   uploads   in   the designated
   conference.    When  an   upload   having   the   prefix   defined in the
   configuration  is  detected,  the FREEDLTEXT will be appended to the file
   description  and  the  file will be made free for downloading.  When this
   occurs the screen will flash and AutoFree will go back to sleep.  Reques-
   ters will notify you of any problems.

